   631	|---|---|---|---|---|
   632	| 1 | A hardened binary node fits k=20 with margin, (a) with three named key sets and no inline work, (b) with one self key and inline work. Name routing works through the public API. | `cost_model` rows of both nodes with the final statement width, canonical disabled slots, carry constraints, type rules; base, unary and binary cases. Rows of R (one and two leaves) and F. Then real proofs with wrong-key, wrong-name and tampered-carry cases through the end. | Any accepted key or name mismatch kills that construction. Above 996,147 rows kills k=20 for that node. No useful inline work (editor's threshold: under 150k rows left) kills the k=20 inline candidate, not GP-4. | 3-7 days of code; modeling 10-60 min, 3-8 GB; proofs 1-3 h, 20-45 GB. |
   633	| 2 | The end closes: one-stage D does not fit three name sets; C plus D does, with no obligation dropped. | Rows, key bytes, proof bytes, time and RSS of D alone and of C then D, over the node of 1. Mutate each carried obligation. | An unauthenticated obligation kills the design. C or D above 2^20 means k=21 for that stage or another split. | 2-5 days after 1; modeling under 1 h; proofs 1-4 h, 20-50 GB. |
   634	| 3 | A ledger-format Compact proof can be verified in circuit. (Astra rank 3; Fable ranked it sixth, as stage 2.) | First, off circuit: reproduce the pinned verifier's challenges and acceptance on a real ZKIR v3 contract proof. Then rows of the keyed Blake2b transcript, complete parsing and point checks in an adapter; the adapter class arch. Beside it: the same circuit re-proved with Poseidon through a plain adapter. | Adapter above 2^20 rows at one verification means splitting it or the general path. A divergence from the native verifier fails. | 1-3 weeks of code; modeling 30-120 min; first proof 2-12 h, 20-60 GB. |
   635	| 4 | Registry and adapter hold against an adversary. | Registered and unregistered inner keys through an admitted adapter; mutated representation and commitment pairs, public-input counts, class, transcript, SRS, kind, root epoch. Count the distinct classes among real Compact circuits (arch, k, input count). | Acceptance of an unregistered inner key or a mismatched normalization kills the interface. Hundreds of classes in practice argues for variable-length absorption or the general path. | 3-7 days beyond 3; proofs 2-8 h. |
   636	| 5 | Committed memory makes the leaf independent of capacity at a useful cost. | Rows of one tagged compression, read, append, stack push, pop and rewrite. Distinct cell accesses per rule from the reference machine, for all four tables, both stacks and the helper record. Same key across tree growth. Canonical result digest across allocation histories. Uses the running 4.1a and E3 results. | A capacity-dependent key, an unauthenticated table, or a median step whose memory rows exceed its rule rows by 10x. | 1-3 weeks for a vertical slice; modeling 30-120 min; proofs 2-8 h. |
   637	| 6 | Typed PCD: coverage, reuse, dependencies, shape and settlement coexist. | Lean and Quint claim layer. Chain, tree, diamond; unary nodes; one-leaf R; alternate bracketings; missing genesis; nonempty dependencies through plain seal; mixed roots; replay across re-batching. Cost of an in-circuit canonical set union against the content-hash root. | Any false sealed claim, undischarged dependency or duplicated effect. Refusing a legitimate shared ancestor also fails. | 4-10 days; model runs 10-60 min; minimal proofs 2-6 h. |
