   648	## 6. Proposed requirements and design changes (text only; no file was changed)
   649	
   650	### 6.1 EARS requirements
   651	
   652	| Id | Text |
   653	|---|---|
   654	| GPR-001 keys | The key set `{U, R, F, N, C, D}` SHALL NOT depend on the program, the input, the run length, the memory size, the registry content, the aggregation shape or its depth. When any of these changes, no key, contract or ceremony SHALL change. |
   655	| GPR-002 node | The node N SHALL verify at most two proofs, each under a key whose transcript representation equals one of the node's public key lanes `n_repr`, `r_repr`, `f_repr`, and SHALL refuse a node with no enabled slot. |
   656	| GPR-003 slot neutrality | When a slot is disabled, the node SHALL fold the canonical neutral accumulator encoding for that slot and SHALL constrain every statement lane of that slot to its canonical empty value. |
   657	| GPR-004 key pinning | The closing proof C SHALL resolve the deferred fixed-base scalars of N, R and F against the constant keys, and the decider D SHALL pin C's key. A proof whose `n_repr`, `r_repr` or `f_repr` differs from the pinned keys SHALL be refused. |
   658	| GPR-005 memory | The leaf U SHALL authenticate every program, input and mutable-memory access against a commitment in its pre-state and SHALL publish the post-state commitment. The leaf relation SHALL NOT contain a constant that bounds the number of program nodes, frames, tasks or table cells below the address width (or, if the owner decides dissent 4 for Astra, at all). |
   659	| GPR-006 genesis | When `h_pre = 0`, the leaf SHALL prove that the pre-state equals `Init(prog_d, input_d)`. The seal rule SHALL require `h_lo = 0`, SHALL open `post_d`, and without a dependency set SHALL require the opened `deps_d` to be the empty commitment. |
   660	| GPR-007 outcomes | The seal rule SHALL accept `Halted(v)` for every value type, `Rejected(code)` and `Exhausted(kind)`, and SHALL publish `out_d = H(outcome_kind, value_d, n_steps)` with `value_d` the digest of the canonical value encoding. A segment whose final state is `Running` SHALL NOT be sealed. |
   661	| GPR-008 height | Owner-step height SHALL be range-checked below 2^64 and SHALL count machine steps only. |
   662	| GPR-009 segments | The node SHALL link two segments only if they have the same `leaf_id`, `prog_d` and `input_d`, `left.post_d = right.pre_d` and `left.h_hi = right.h_lo`. |
   663	| GPR-010 claims | A claim SHALL be `H(CLAIM, kind, id, in_d, out_d)`. A set statement SHALL be `(set_root, n_claims)` where `set_root` is computed in circuit from the children's roots with domain-separated tags for claim leaf, join and dependency. |
   664	| GPR-011 consumption | When a run consumes claims, its state SHALL carry the commitment `deps_d` to them, and the run SHALL be sealed only together with a verified set whose root equals `deps_d`. |
   665	| GPR-012 registry | The foreign lift F SHALL compute `vk_id` from the witnessed adapter key, SHALL prove membership of `(vk_id, kind)` and of the adapter's published inner `vk_id` under `reg_root`, SHALL resolve the witnessed key's commitments in circuit, and SHALL fold the adapter's published accumulator with the adapter proof's own. `vk_id` SHALL bind the arch, k, exact public-input count, format versions, transcript and SRS identity. |
   666	| GPR-012b run entry | The seal rule SHALL prove that the Sherlock leaf identity carried by the segment is a registry member of kind `run` under `reg_root`. |
   667	| GPR-013 registry root | Every node SHALL require its children to carry its own `reg_root`. The contract SHALL accept a root only if the proof's `reg_root` equals the contract's registry root. |
   668	| GPR-014 adapters | An adapter SHALL prepare one proof of its class under a witnessed key with the exact public-input count of that key, SHALL publish that key's `vk_id`, the digest of the complete public-input vector and the resulting accumulator, and SHALL NOT publish a value that is not a public input or an opened commitment. |
   669	| GPR-015 format | Where a claim asserts that ledger proof bytes were verified, the adapter SHALL enforce the ledger transcript, encodings, instance layout and complete parsing. Where the proof was made with another transcript under the same key, the claim kind SHALL say so. |
   670	| GPR-016 shape | The decided statement SHALL carry `set_root`, binding the claim DAG by content, and `shape_d`, binding the proof graph including slot bits, unary nodes and segment bracketing. Acceptance SHALL NOT depend on an off-chain manifest. |
   671	| GPR-017 completeness | The decider SHALL refuse a root that is not a set statement. |
   672	| GPR-018 settlement | The contract SHALL accept each decided root at most once and SHALL record each opened claim at most once, keyed by the claim identifier, whatever root it is opened from. |
   673	| GPR-019 size | The final proof and the decider's public-input count SHALL be the same for every shape, depth and number of claims. |
