openspec/changes/sherlock-vm-consensus-20261107/dissent.md:112:None. The concerns every member asked to carry forward are recorded as implementation limits, not dissent: the genesis realization must be re-justified at the re-pinned `midnight-circuits 7.3.0` before node keygen (task 2.3; fable-2 prefers realization (b)); the universal soundness/completeness obligations O1-O4 stay open until a theorem exists; the universal leaf k, prover memory for S>1 and complete-path cost are unmeasured; the deployed node source for spec 2001100 is not public (SMN-004 limit). A council vote is not proof execution, deployment acceptance or a release.
openspec/changes/sherlock-vm-consensus-20261107/dissent.md:158:1. **Throughput is mandatory.** SRC-011 moves from Optional to Ubiquitous with the owner's caps: under 2 h wall, under 48 GB peak RSS per process, under 100 GB aggregate across the concurrent heavy processes of a run; a shortfall is a failing row, never a pass by being recorded. This supersedes the ISSUE 9 reading ("shortfall reporting closes measurement only") in the stronger direction: the measurement tasks still close on a recorded shortfall, but the throughput rows (A18, A19, A19b) then fail and gate G-C blocks OP-PV-DEPLOY. Staged gates SRC-015: node step at k=19 <= 60 s / 16 GB (A16), `entry 7;` under 20 min (A18, G-B), fact(3) and list123 under 2 h (A19, A19b, G-C). Caps are seeded requirement caps (`fixed: true`), not measured-then-doubled.
openspec/changes/sherlock-vm-consensus-20261107/dissent.md:162:5. **One general aggregation model (SRC-017).** Segment composition is modeled once, the linear chain being the degenerate tree: a Quint model (`models/sherlock/quint/aggregation.qnt`, constants `TREE` and `S`, F20) and Lean theorems (`clean/fork/Clean/Sherlock/Aggregation.lean` in `SherlockSpec`, F21) cover linkage and associativity, padding and identity neutrality, exactly-once coverage, height bounds, unique genesis, replay, schedule independence, program fixity, shape binding, independence from shape and S, and "the root statement implies a valid execution of the general machine for every program". One fixed key set serves every program and every step count. The tools are the `quint-modeling`, `quint-lang` and `quint-execute-spec` skills and the lean4 plugin of the workflowskills repo. A council review (skill `council`, cross-family lanes; task 2.14) of the design plus the formal results precedes the implementation of the node constraints (2.3), the S-slot leaf (4.2) and any tree node (5.7).
openspec/changes/sherlock-vm-consensus-20261107/dissent.md:164:7. **New task order (tasks.md).** 2.1 -> 1.9 -> 2.0 -> the C0 path (2.7, 2.8, 2.9, 2.13) and the formal tasks (2.11, 2.12) in parallel -> 2.14 -> G-A -> 2.3 -> 2.4 -> 2.5 -> 2.6 -> GPU phases if open; M4 chooses S at G-A' before the leaf is keyed; M5 carries the throughput gates G-B and G-C; 6.2 depends on G-C. Each task is marked **[loop]** (unattended), **[lead]** (gate or decision) or **[owner]** (install or spend). Gate decisions are committed JSON under `qa/sherlock/decisions/` (`speed-levers.json`).
openspec/changes/sherlock-vm-consensus-20261107/dissent.md:175:- The owner said (verbatim): "We don't care about stagenet anymore, Midnight forked, this can work on mainnet. We should test on preview or preprod (whichever is the canonical test infrastructure)."
openspec/changes/sherlock-vm-consensus-20261107/dissent.md:190:1. **Genesis guarantee (open; review §4.2 dissent 2; design §3.2(5), SRC-021).** Which mechanism establishes that a run starts from the canonical initial state of its program: option G1, an in-circuit first-leaf check selected by `h_pre == 0` or another authenticated mechanism; or option G2, off-chain recomputation of `init_d` by the independent verifier, with O1 restated so that an `acceptRun` is a claim relative to the sealed `init_d`. The editor of the review held G2 acceptable if O1 and task 4.9 are rewritten. The second reviewer (review §4.2 dissent 2) held that G2 is sound only for a verifier that performs the recomputation: any reader or downstream contract that treats an `acceptRun` as proof of a canonical run can be fooled, because the constructor accepts any nonzero digest (`tools/sherlock-sdk/sherlock-run.compact:29-38`), and for an unauthenticated `init_d` the Lean premise may not hold. **Lead recommendation:** G1, the in-circuit or otherwise authenticated mechanism (the second reviewer's position), with its cost measured by experiment E3 (task 4.13) before the choice is final. The choice is needed before 4.2 because it changes `k_U`.
openspec/changes/sherlock-vm-consensus-20261107/dissent.md:192:3. **No S >= 4 fallback (open; restates item 3 of "Owner decisions still open after 2026-11-08 (3)"; review C3).** If no S >= 4 fits the measured leaf, node and decider caps, what follows. Option F (S=1, about 5 h on the node chain alone), the tree (k=21, F22) and the GPU backend (unbuilt, unfunded, no measured gain) are not available answers today. **Lead recommendation (from review C3):** the leaf design is revisited before any key; S <= 2 is a redesign trigger; G-C stays as written (2 h, 48 GB per process, 100 GB aggregate), and a recorded shortfall is not a pass.
openspec/changes/sherlock-vm-consensus-20261107/tasks.md:5:Who runs what (2026-11-08 (3)): **[loop]** tasks run unattended by the work loop under their budget caps; **[lead]** tasks need a lead decision (the gates G-A, G-A', G-B, G-C, the k=19 cut, the U/F choice (option F not planned since 2026-11-10), time boxes, statement reviews); **[owner]** tasks need an install or a spend. Principles (`order.md` §4): measurements before optimizations; a gate between each measurement and the optimization it licenses; the soundness fixes (2.3) and the k=19 cut in one change so 2.4 keys once; S chosen before the universal leaf is keyed so 4.4 keys once; the formal design work (2.11, 2.12, 2.14) before the node constraints, the S-slot leaf and any tree node are implemented (SRC-017); tree and GPU as measured options behind their rows; no heavy run before 2.0 (F18) has landed (SRC-016).
