openspec/changes/sherlock-vm-consensus-20261107/design.md:22:| D13' | Tree aggregation (amended 2026-11-08 (3); owner: "reopen tree aggregation"): the uniform three-slot self-recursive node of `tree.md` F8 (one key `SHKTRE01`; slots left-self, right-self, leaf, each gated by a bit; a disabled slot is the identity segment; an all-disabled node is refused; genesis check moves to the decider `root.pre_d == init_d`, `root.h_lo == 0`; the tree manifest is hash-bound into the bundle and `verify_chain` replays the exact slot order). The per-level-key fallback of `stagenet-gp-recursion.md:168` is struck: it violates SRC-017 | Measured option (was Cut); built only if the G-A/G-B criteria of §3.5 pass | `tree.md` §7 criteria: slot node <= 0.95 x 2^20 rows (F22); f3 <= 1.4 or U <= 6 cores at 20 threads and aggregate <= 100 GB (A23); projected ceil(L/3) x t x f3 <= 0.5 x L x t; owner's 100 GB aggregate and E11 (met by decision). It was the lever if `k_U >= 18` or k=19 fails, or if the chain alone misses the target (`prover.md` §6). Closed by F22 (k=21); a chain shortfall does not reopen it (amended 2026-11-10). This closes only the three-slot node of `tree.md` F8; GP-4 (any shape) stays the target through task 4.14. |
openspec/changes/sherlock-vm-consensus-20261107/design.md:29:The source fragment is literals, variables, let, checked UInt128/Bool primitives, conditional, named call, constructor and ordered match (`design.md:11`). State is control, environment, ordered frames, values, outcome, fuel and counters (`interfaces.md:55-88`). A step is one owner-engine event; helpers in `/1` are explicit bounded microsteps with cursors (`interfaces.md:92-96`). Outcomes: `Running | Halted(v) | Rejected(code) | Exhausted(kind)`. Error codes 4 (frame cap), 9 (no match), 10 (checked arithmetic) are fixed (`interfaces.md:7`).
openspec/changes/sherlock-vm-consensus-20261107/design.md:31:Physical layout `sherlock-c6-phys/1`: image header 48 lanes, control 17 lanes, frames 13 lanes each bottom-to-top, sections META/PROG/CTX/IMAGE/DATA/HELPER (`c6_phys.rs:1-30`, `c6_phys_host.rs:1-30`). `StepInv` holds between canonical boundaries: data arena append-only and child-before-parent, frames and helper slots zeroed on release, inactive fields zero (`interfaces.md:177-193`). `decodeCanonical` only at genesis, `ChunkStore`, checkpoint resume and external claims; `decodeStep` mid-run. Internal microsteps preserve `StepInv` without canonical projection (astra-2 SND-002; `security-candidate-b.md:A4`).
openspec/changes/sherlock-vm-consensus-20261107/design.md:50:Soundness premises carried from the per-rule design: canonicality of the pre IMAGE/HELPER/DATA sections is enforced by the gated fragment on the same lanes; PROG canonicality by the parser walk. Putting dispatch and fragments inside one key makes the "caller obligation" at `c6_dispatch_step.rs:34-38` checkable, not discharged: SAS-010 requires, for every admitted rule, evidence that `StepInv` is initialized at canonical genesis, preserved by the gated fragment under `StepInv(pre)`, and that every fragment premise refers to the shared carriers (no disconnected copies). Task 4.6 covers initialization as well as hostile transitions (astra-2).
openspec/changes/sherlock-vm-consensus-20261107/design.md:54:A leaf proves `S >= 1` consecutive owner steps on one key. Inside the leaf: `pre_0` is the digested `pre_d`; for `i < S-1`, `post_i == pre_{i+1}` lane by lane; `post_{S-1}` is digested as `post_d`. `steps` is the number of *enabled* owner-step events in the leaf; a short final chunk pads with disabled steps (`enable == 0`, identity on lanes, zero contribution to `steps`). Terminal: a step that publishes (`Halted`, `Rejected`, `Exhausted`) is the last enabled step; later slots are disabled. Charged work and fuel stay inside the state digest; `steps` and `h` are physical counts (ISSUE 5).
openspec/changes/sherlock-vm-consensus-20261107/design.md:56:S rule (amended 2026-11-10, review C3 and §5 design edit 2; replaces the 2026-11-08 (3) rule `k_U + log2 S <= 20`): the leaf is U. S and the worker count are chosen at G-A' from measurements of the complete admitted relation and of the node and decider keyed over a leaf of its arch. `k_U + log2 S <= K_LEAF_MAX` is a first sizing estimate. `K_LEAF_MAX` is the largest leaf k the leaf prover accepts within 16 GB: `K_LEAF_MAX` = [PENDING experiment E4: k=20 leaf prove time and RSS, task 4.11]. The wrapper cap is 19 today (`crates/mori-backend/src/proving.rs:22`, `sherlock_c6_child.rs:868,880`); it is a wrapper constant, not an upstream limit. S >= 8 is the planning target. S=4 may be chosen only with a measured leaf time. S <= 2 does not meet G-C at the measured node step and is a redesign trigger. If no S >= 4 fits, the leaf design is revisited before any key. S is a power of two and at most `S_MAX` = 16 (§3.2(1)). S=1 is the one-enabled-slot case of the same relation, not a separate baseline. The leaf is built with S slots (4.2) and keyed once (4.4). The node-only arithmetic is the table in §3.5. Leaf rows grow about S-fold (`k_leaf = k_U + ceil(log2 S)`), prove time about S x t_step, RSS about S x RSS(k_U); the leaf's private witness holds S copies of the carriers; the measured leaf k, time and RSS at the chosen S are recorded at 4.4 (row A20) and the cap is 16 GB per leaf prover so two or three leaf workers fit beside the node under the 100 GB aggregate (open question Q4).
