openspec/changes/sherlock-vm-consensus-20261107/design.md:85:Measured at the ledger 9.1.0.1 pins (amended 2026-11-10, review §5 design edit 6): node `SHKIVC06` k=20, 652,437 rows over the stand-in leaf (`qa/sherlock/decisions/speed-levers.json` `node_rows_at_7_3_0`) and 741,708 over the k=13 C6 digest-leaf key (`qa/sherlock/manifests/node.json` `model_rows`); run decider 929,166 rows over that node (`qa/sherlock/manifests/run-decider.json` `model_rows`), 119,410 under 2^20; node step 59.6-63.6 s, 16.6-17.4 GB, decider 70.35 s, all with stand-in leaves (task 2.6, row A16). The leaf key alone adds 89,271 node rows, so a wider leaf key can push the decider to k=21 while the leaf itself fits. The largest leaf key for which node and decider stay at k=20 is [PENDING experiment E2, task 4.12]. The 2026-11-07 figures at `8fd34ed79` (node 531,989 rows, about 95 s/step at 4 threads, 26.2 GB; decider 833,235 rows; `stagenet-gp-recursion.md:184-201`) are history. The primary path (2026-11-08 (3)) is this chain with S-batched leaves and 2-3 parallel leaf workers proving ahead of the node chain under the 100 GB aggregate cap (`prover.md` F11: leaves are independent, so with P workers `T ~ max(N x t_node, N x t_leaf / P) + t_node + t_decider` and the wall is the node chain alone while `k_U <= 17`). The tree node of D13' would be a different node statement and key; it is closed by F22 (k=21), so it is not an alternative for the node layer today (§3.5 lever 5). This closes only the three-slot node of `tree.md` F8; GP-4 (any shape) stays the target through task 4.14.
openspec/changes/sherlock-vm-consensus-20261107/design.md:90:2. Genesis: `is_genesis = is_zero(prev_h)`; require `prev_d == init_d` (exists, `ivc.rs:312-313`). Today `proof_acc` is scaled by `not_genesis` (`ivc.rs:343`) while the witness-supplied `prev_acc` is folded unscaled (`:318-327,364`). The normative requirement is UISEC-010: no unauthenticated deferred obligation at genesis. The implementation must either (a) constrain the supplied carry to the designated neutral encoding at genesis, or (b) constrain a zero/ignore construction (scale `prev_acc` by `not_genesis`) and justify that it cannot authorize an invalid leaf or predecessor. Tests match the chosen semantics: non-neutral refusal for (a); semantic irrelevance of a well-formed ignored carry for (b), without requiring identical folded bytes (ignored inputs may still alter transcript encodings); and invalid-leaf refusal through the final pairing for both. Retaining an unscaled supplied carry requires a separately recorded security argument. The target implementation hashes accumulator encodings before deriving folding powers (`circuits/src/verifier/accumulator.rs:177-192,315-343` at `24a1eb5a`, astra-2); this is a transcript observation, not a proof that cancellation is impossible. Malformed point-encoding refusal is classified at its actual boundary. No practical attack was demonstrated; this is hardening (astra-2, fable-2).
openspec/changes/sherlock-vm-consensus-20261107/design.md:91:   **Chosen 2026-11-09 (task 2.3, node `SHKIVC06`): realization (a).** The node computes the public encoding of the carried accumulator once (`verifier.as_public_input`, the same lanes `prev_pi` absorbs and `accumulate` hashes at `midnight-circuits 7.3.0`, `verifier/accumulator.rs` `AssignedAccumulator::accumulate`) and constrains `is_genesis * (lane - neutral) == 0` for every lane, `neutral` the encoding of `trivial_acc` (`ivc.rs` `constrain_genesis_neutral`); the host `next_acc` refuses a non-neutral genesis carry too. Why (a): it is cheap (one multiply-add and one zero assertion per lane, about 60 lanes, no new MSM; the carry check measures 2,106 rows with the carried accumulator assignment, while a second `collapse` of `prev_acc`, as realization (b) would need, is a variable-base MSM like `collapse_self`, which measures 239,577 rows), it needs no new security argument, and it removes the hash from the argument entirely: at genesis the carry and the collapsed scaled `proof_acc` both equal `trivial_acc`, whose MSMs are the identity on both sides, so the folded value is `r^2 * leaf_acc` plus identity terms and the pairing holds iff the leaf's does (for `r != 0`), while the fold challenge is a function of the leaf alone (no grinding freedom). Model match: the Quint F20 `accOf` folds no carry for a genesis node (`al = []`); the circuit folds `[trivial, trivial, leaf]`, which equals that fold up to neutral terms. Lean (council fixes, `bd7703f4d`): the node fold is `AccAlgebra.nodeFold b p c l = collapse (accumulate [collapse (scale b p), collapse (scale b c), l])` and the genesis lemma is `genesis_collapse_both` (it replaces `genesis_scale_by_bit`). The circuit realizes `nodeFold` on every accepted witness: `p` is scaled by `not_genesis` and collapsed (`collapse_self`); `c` is constrained to collapsed form at every height (scalar one per side, `constrain_collapsed_carry`, so `collapse c = c` and no second MSM is needed) and to the `trivial_acc` encoding at genesis (`= collapse (scale false c)` by `collapse_scale_false`); the fold and the final collapse are the same. The range checks are the contract of `src004_height_bridge` (raw `prev_h`, `steps`, `h` below 2^64, `1 <= steps <= S`), and the linear node statement maps to the F21 chain by `lin_refines_chain`. Malformed carry encodings are refused at their decoder boundary (`acc_from_lanes`, decoder evidence only).
openspec/changes/sherlock-vm-consensus-20261107/design.md:94:5. Canonical initialization (amended 2026-11-10, review §5 design edit 4 and dissent 2; SRC-021). Today the node checks `prev_d == init_d` only (`ivc.rs:498-501`), the contract constructor checks `init_d != 0` only (`tools/sherlock-sdk/sherlock-run.compact:29-38`), and Lean `leaf_sound` and `decider_pinning` take a carrier state opening `init_d` as a premise (`Aggregation.lean:204-213,1110-1120`). Initialization also takes fuel and a stack limit (`crates/mori-core/src/sherlock/reference.rs:14`), so a function of the program image alone is not enough. Equality with a supplied `init_d` alone establishes neither option below. Mechanism: [PENDING owner question 1 of `dissent.md` "Owner questions from the 2026-11-10 design review"], one of:
openspec/changes/sherlock-vm-consensus-20261107/design.md:95:   - Option G1, in-circuit or otherwise authenticated: a first-leaf check selected by `h_pre == 0` proves that `pre` is the canonical initial state for the program image, configuration, fuel and stack limit that `prog_d` commits. Its row cost is [PENDING experiment E3, task 4.13].
openspec/changes/sherlock-vm-consensus-20261107/design.md:96:   - Option G2, off-chain recomputation: the independent verifier (SRC-010) recomputes `init_d` from program, configuration, fuel and stack limit; an `acceptRun` is then a claim relative to the sealed `init_d`, and O1 (`assurance.md`) is restated.
openspec/changes/sherlock-vm-consensus-20261107/design.md:100:The decider verifies the last node proof, pins `vk_N_repr`, folds and pairs the accumulator, opens `cur_d = Poseidon(SHK_SD, HALTED, result, lanes_d)` and binds `values`. The outcome tag and result are derived from the proved state, not supplied as constants (astra-2 SND-004; `sherlock_c6_child.rs:560`). `acceptRun` reads sealed `program_d` and `init_d`, refuses replay of `stmt`, writes `result` as big-endian `Bytes<16>` (`sherlock-run.compact:26-47`). The acceptRun transcript template (70 slots, `tests/fixtures/run-template.json`) is recaptured with Compact 0.36.0 / runtime 0.21.0 and diffed against `template.rs` (SMN-003).
