openspec/changes/sherlock-vm-consensus-20261107/requirements.md:10:| SVM-002 | S | While a run is between canonical boundaries, every accepted step SHALL preserve `StepInv` (append-only data arena, child-before-parent, zeroed released slots, zero inactive fields) given `StepInv(pre)`, and canonical genesis SHALL establish it; canonical decoding applies only at genesis, chunk store, resume and external claims. | Initialization: canonical genesis admitted, non-canonical refused. Preservation, raw-witness hostile cases (inactive-slot garbage, referenced unreachable node, foreign codeId, tag/layout mismatch, write below activeLength, nondeterministic post-image, Return payload/padding copied at publication): each is refused by the leaf key, or a checked argument shows the pre-state violates `StepInv` and is unreachable from canonical genesis; the record names which. A bad pre-state outside `StepInv` is not by itself a full-run exploit. | UISEC-002..005; `security-candidate-b.md:A4`; SND-002; SAS-010; D2 |
openspec/changes/sherlock-vm-consensus-20261107/requirements.md:27:| SRC-005 | X | If `prev_h == 0` (genesis), the node SHALL require `prev_d == init_d` and SHALL introduce no unauthenticated deferred obligation, by realization (a) constraining the supplied carry to the designated neutral encoding, or (b) constraining a zero/ignore construction (carry scaled by `not_genesis`) with a recorded justification that an ignored carry cannot authorize an invalid leaf or predecessor; retaining an unscaled supplied carry requires a separately recorded security argument (the `24a1eb5a` hash observation is an input to it, not the argument). | Per the chosen realization, from a valid baseline at the node constraint boundary: (a) a non-neutral carry is refused; (b) two genesis proofs differing only in a well-formed ignored carry both pass the decider (identical folded bytes not required); in both, an invalid leaf accumulator at genesis is refused through the final pairing, and a malformed carry encoding is refused at its decoder boundary (decoder evidence only). The choice is recorded before node keygen (task 2.3). No practical attack was demonstrated; this is hardening. | UISEC-010; ZR04/ZR08; SND-003; `ivc.rs:318-364`; §3.2(2) |
