openspec/changes/sherlock-vm-consensus-20261107/requirements.md:33:| SRC-011 | U | (Mandatory since 2026-11-08 (3); was O.) A committed program of at most 320 owner steps SHALL prove its leaves, fold them through the node chain or the tree, prove the run decider, pass the independent verifier (SRC-010) and the local proof-verifying `validate_call` (SRC-020) in under 2 h wall, under 48 GB peak RSS per process and under 100 GB aggregate peak RSS across the concurrently running heavy processes of the run (owner decision 2026-11-08: "48 GB per process, 100 GB aggregate"), on the 20-core 120 GB host, as one `heavy` run or a declared concurrent set of runs whose wall is the makespan; the receipt SHALL record `RAYON_NUM_THREADS`, the concurrency P and both peaks. The C0 phase profile (RPP) SHALL be committed before any S, concurrency, GPU or tree adoption, and each adoption SHALL cite the C0 metric that justified it (`qa/sherlock/decisions/speed-levers.json`). A shortfall is a failing row; it never passes by being recorded. (Amended 2026-11-10.) A projection SHALL use total wall = setup + max(node service, leaf service) under measured mixed contention + decider + independent verification (SRC-010) + call validation (SRC-020); a lever that is not built and measured SHALL get no credit in G-C. | `budgets.json` rows `chain-entry7`, `chain-fact3`, `chain-list123` (caps seeded, SRC-015); rows A18, A19, A19b; `qa/sherlock/decisions/speed-levers.json` names the C0 metric behind every adopted lever. | RPP-001..010; CONSENSUS C0; owner decision 2026-11-08 (3) "way too slow" |
openspec/changes/sherlock-vm-consensus-20261107/requirements.md:37:| SRC-015 | U | Staged throughput (added 2026-11-08 (3)). (a) After the node fixes and the k=19 cut (task 2.3), one node step SHALL prove in at most 60 s and 16 GB peak RSS at the qualification thread count, or the shortfall and its C0 phase cause SHALL be recorded and S raised at gate G-A (row A16, budget `node-k19-step`). (b) The `entry 7;` chain (6 owner steps) SHALL complete end to end (leaves, node chain or tree, decider, `verify_chain`, `validate_call`) in under 20 min, 48 GB per process, 100 GB aggregate (row A18, budget `chain-entry7`; gate G-B). (c) fact(3) (293 steps) and list123 (303 steps) SHALL each complete in under 2 h, 48 GB per process, 100 GB aggregate (rows A19, A19b, budgets `chain-fact3`, `chain-list123`; gate G-C, which blocks OP-PV-DEPLOY). Caps are seeded requirement caps (`fixed: true`), never measured-then-doubled; a shortfall is a failing row. | `budgets.json` keys `node-k19-step`, `chain-entry7`, `chain-fact3`, `chain-list123` carry `cap` with `fixed: true`; `heavy` enforces the seeded cap (task 2.0 makes `limits_for` honour a fixed cap with `measured` null); rows A16, A18, A19, A19b pass under them. | SRC-011; `order.md` §3.1, §3.3; `prover.md` §2, §6 (k19 node ESTIMATE 48-55 s, ~13 GB) |
openspec/changes/sherlock-vm-consensus-20261107/requirements.md:39:| SRC-017 | U | General-purpose recursion with fixed keys and formal gates (owner decision 2026-11-08: "It has to be general purpose recursion"; "have some agents explore it with lean and quint"). (Amended 2026-11-10, owner: "It needs to be general purpose recursion. Make sure we understand what that means. And universal".) The target SHALL be GP-1 to GP-4 as defined in `general-purpose.md` (GP-001..GP-004); the design of this change is the first milestone toward GP-1, and its open gaps are listed in design §3.6. The clauses below state what the first milestone SHALL meet. The leaf, node and decider keys SHALL be independent of the program, the initial state, the step count, the fold schedule and the tree shape: one key set (leaf over the frozen inventory `R` at the keyed S, one self-recursive node, one decider, one acceptRun template) serves every committed program; S is a keyed constant; the node is self-recursive under its own key (linear chain or the uniform three-slot tree node of `tree.md` F8, in which disabled slots are the identity and the tree manifest is hash-bound); per-program, per-depth or per-level keys are refused. One general aggregation model SHALL cover both shapes (the linear chain is the degenerate tree): a Quint model `models/sherlock/quint/aggregation.qnt` (constant `TREE`, constant S) whose invariants (linkage and associativity, padding and identity neutrality, exactly-once coverage, height bounds and monotonicity, unique genesis, replay, schedule independence, program fixity, shape binding, fixed keys, liveness witness) pass with every seeded mutant caught, and Lean theorems in `clean/fork/Clean/Sherlock/Aggregation.lean` (library `SherlockSpec`, statement/axiom split) that build with zero `sorry` and whose `#print axioms` lists only the declared premises: segment soundness for every program ("the root statement implies a valid execution of the general machine for every program"), associativity of linkage, padding neutrality, exactly-once coverage, height arithmetic without wrap, decider pinning, independence from shape, depth and S. The Quint and Lean rows (F20, F21) and a council review of the design plus the formal results SHALL pass before the node constraints (2.3), the S-slot leaf (4.2) or any tree node (5.7) are implemented. | `write_relation` bytes of node and decider contain the leaf VK and k only (a program-dependent constant is a defect); F20 `quint test` passes, every mutant caught, with `TREE=false` and `TREE=true`; F21 `lake build SherlockSpec` in `clean/fork` passes with zero `sorry` and the axiom list within the premise file (`scripts/qa/check-lean-aggregation.sh`, exit 2 while the toolchain is absent); tasks 2.3, 4.2 and 5.7 list F20 and F21 in `depends`; the council review record (task 2.14) is committed. | owner decisions 2026-11-08 (3); `order.md` §1b; `tree.md` §3, §4; `prover.md` §6a, §6b; SAS-009 |
openspec/changes/sherlock-vm-consensus-20261107/requirements.md:43:| SRC-021 | X | (Added 2026-11-10.) If a run's initial carriers are not the canonical initial state for the program image, configuration, fuel and stack limit that `prog_d` commits, the run SHALL NOT be accepted as a canonical run; equality with a supplied `init_d` alone SHALL NOT count as that check. The mechanism is [PENDING owner question 1 of `dissent.md` "Owner questions from the 2026-11-10 design review"]: option G1, an in-circuit or otherwise authenticated first-leaf check selected by `h_pre == 0` (cost [PENDING experiment E3, task 4.13]), or option G2, off-chain recomputation of `init_d` by the independent verifier with O1 restated. | Under the chosen mechanism: non-canonical genesis carriers, an `init_d` inconsistent with `prog_d`, and forged initial carriers are refused at the named boundary (row A13); the record names which circuit or verifier performs the check. | design review 2026-11-10 C2, dissent 2; O1; SAS-010 |
