The measured dispatch block alone is too large, so changing which key verifies it does not solve the leaf-cost problem. I’m leaning toward an inline processor with authenticated memory and specialised tables. Its main uncertainty is the full recursion cost: added tables can enlarge the node’s verifying key and decider, even if execution gets cheaper.
