    24	**Task A. Findings on Fable’s proposal**
    25	
    26	**A.1. Named lifts can share verification logic, subject to an exact class match**
    27	
    28	**Claim:** N, R and F can use one polymorphic verifier slot because they share a constraint system and k. [F1:160]
    29	
    30	**Verdict: CONFIRMED, conditionally.**
    31	
    32	`AssignedVk` keeps the domain and constraint system outside the circuit. Its only assigned key field is `transcript_repr`. `MidnightVK::read` reconstructs its constraint system from the architecture and k. This supports a common verifier for different keys generated through the same stdlib configuration. [MC:verifier/mod.rs:55, MC:verifier/verifier_gadget.rs:207, ZS:lib.rs:1573]
    33	
